  "title": "# Build: terminal-vps-host (Current profile) - URGENT ops fix Brett, Nov 3 2026: the console Termin…",
  "asked": "# Build: terminal-vps-host (Current profile) - URGENT ops fix Brett, Nov 3 2026: the console Terminal shows NO headless tabs. `console-terminal/headless` read returns `{ready:false, items:[], why:\"the VPS tab isn't set up (Settings -> Plugins -> Terminal -> VPS host)\"}`. So headless-tabs (PR #259, live) can't attach to any build's tmux session. Assigned agent: whoever is free (all-rounder router if on main; else book on **Ping Paulie**; record who). Register in the `current` profile (id `terminal-vps-host`) + banner entry. Fix right away, tell after. ## Do - s1 Find how the Terminal plugin (apps/console-web/plugins/console-terminal or terminal) stores the VPS host connection and what it needs (host, user, port, SSH key/agent). Configure it for the axf-console container to reach the VPS host (same Hostinger VPS: host.docker.internal / docker gateway / the VPS address) as root with a dedicated [hidden] an ed25519 key for the console, add its public key to /root/.ssh/authorized_keys (restricted is fine), store the private key in the console's secure store / a mounted secret (never in the repo, never echoed in logs). - s2 Make the setting persistent across container redeploys (Coolify env/secret or mounted volume) so Lenny's landings don't wipe it. If Coolify config is needed, document it and use the existing Coolify API path (COOLIFY_TOKEN) if available. - s3 Verify: `console-terminal/headless` returns ready:true and lists the running axf-* tmux sessions (toolbar-tap-confirm, crew-live, auto-land-2, ui-review-shots, follow-amber, claude-settings, ...); meters return cost; opening the Terminal auto-opens a tab per build with agent + model + live cost. - s4 Add a health@1 check: red when the Terminal VPS host isn't ready, with Auto fix. Systems check banner row. - s5 Report `_claude/builds/reports/terminal-vps-host.md`, THREADS, PR, steps through the store. Commits clean and professional. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
